(2001038, 276150, 43551, '<td valign="top">great usage of shapes!!!</td>', 'great usage of shapes!!!', '2006-01-04 01:19:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001050, 276022, 43463, '<td valign="top">The main subject is what really captures and holds the eye''s attention. Love how you effectively captured the light coming off this light fixture - the light flows off and accents the curves of the piece as well as the shadows. I have two critiques on this piece. First the stem of the light fixture is too distracting - the more you can eliminate from changing the angle the better it would be. Speaking of changing the angle if you had angled the shot such that the main light fixture remains in the center with the background showing "two triangles" dividing the rectangle format you would have captured a multitude of interesting shapes that all complimented each other. Had you angled the line between wall and ceiling to match up with the opposite corners of the rectangle format of this photo it would have created the illusion of a trianglated background - one light brown the other chocolate brown.</td>', 'The main subject is what really captures and holds the eye''s attention. Love how you effectively captured the light coming off this light fixture - the light flows off and accents the curves of the piece as well as the shadows. I have two critiques on this piece. First the stem of the light fixture is too distracting - the more you can eliminate from changing the angle the better it would be. Speaking of changing the angle if you had angled the shot such that the main light fixture remains in the center with the background showing "two triangles" dividing the rectangle format you would have captured a multitude of interesting shapes that all complimented each other. Had you angled the line between wall and ceiling to match up with the opposite corners of the rectangle format of this photo it would have created the illusion of a trianglated background - one light brown the other chocolate brown.', '2006-01-04 01:21:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001055, 275637, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is interesting and it''s very nicely done in DOF and light/luminance. It lacks a defining shape, however, as if it were more of a "pattern" picture. I feel a need for the shape itself to be more dominant in this particular challenge.</td>', 'This is interesting and it''s very nicely done in DOF and light/luminance. It lacks a defining shape, however, as if it were more of a "pattern" picture. I feel a need for the shape itself to be more dominant in this particular challenge.', '2006-01-04 01:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
