(2008915, 274356, 50715, '<td valign="top">Image contains some pixelation - maybe too much compression or taken on too small resolution?<br/> <br/>Even more importantly, the centre of interest (the ball) is out of focus while some of the leaves in the right of the photo are in focus - so there is competition for attention.  If the ball was inside your minimum focus length, then maybe you should have moved back a bit and then cropped?  Or alternatively, deliberately made the entire image out of focus (e.g. by focusing on infinity) which would make the leaves very blurry and let the coloured shapes dominate?</td>', 'Image contains some pixelation - maybe too much compression or taken on too small resolution? Even more importantly, the centre of interest (the ball) is out of focus while some of the leaves in the right of the photo are in focus - so there is competition for attention.  If the ball was inside your minimum focus length, then maybe you should have moved back a bit and then cropped?  Or alternatively, deliberately made the entire image out of focus (e.g. by focusing on infinity) which would make the leaves very blurry and let the coloured shapes dominate?', '2006-01-06 00:38:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2009103, 276456, 20168, '<td valign="top">Classic Oregon Coast photo! Great entry into this challenge. Indeed, we see one of the best known iconic shapes from entire the pacific coastline, Canada to Mexico, Haystack Rock. Excellent composition, with every quadrant in the rule of thirds offering the eye a different portion of the whole. The people in the lower right put the whole scene into perspective. 10!</td>', 'Classic Oregon Coast photo! Great entry into this challenge. Indeed, we see one of the best known iconic shapes from entire the pacific coastline, Canada to Mexico, Haystack Rock. Excellent composition, with every quadrant in the rule of thirds offering the eye a different portion of the whole. The people in the lower right put the whole scene into perspective. 10!', '2006-01-06 02:02:15.000000', NULL, 1),
