(2026967, 274199, 16046, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m relieved that I finally got a ribbon under my belt. Thanks everyone for all the great comments. My better half, Ling-Ling wanted me to shoot her little cup and I thought it looked like one of those fat exhaust pipes you see on Honda cars when you tilted it. And yes, multiple exposures are legal as long as they are done inside the camera. This DPC club has such tough competition, which make us all better photographers.<br/> <br/>Frank</td>', 'Wow, I''m relieved that I finally got a ribbon under my belt. Thanks everyone for all the great comments. My better half, Ling-Ling wanted me to shoot her little cup and I thought it looked like one of those fat exhaust pipes you see on Honda cars when you tilted it. And yes, multiple exposures are legal as long as they are done inside the camera. This DPC club has such tough competition, which make us all better photographers. Frank', '2006-01-11 14:59:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2027021, 276454, 49598, '<td valign="top">Congrats! I didn''t get a chance to vote but this is impressive...<br/> <br/>"the female of the species is more deadly than the male..." - was that a kipling reference or from the band space? Either way, I would like to see what that picture would have looked like...</td>', 'Congrats! I didn''t get a chance to vote but this is impressive... "the female of the species is more deadly than the male..." - was that a kipling reference or from the band space? Either way, I would like to see what that picture would have looked like...', '2006-01-11 15:14:43.000000', NULL, 0),
