(2057934, 274636, 17850, '<td valign="top">Thank you Alice and all of you people for you comments!<br/>As Astronomy is my major interest (side by side with Photography of course!), this is one more "astro"-photo related with our parent star''s destiny. There was not muct post processing at this image, Mainly the camera''s settings helped to capture this specific view. <br/>But you can''t imagine how impressive and spectacular it was in my eyes also. The clouds were moving just at the edge of the road, and Sun''s light gave them an orange color... amazing. Fortunately I was lucky enough to keep this moment!</td>', 'Thank you Alice and all of you people for you comments!As Astronomy is my major interest (side by side with Photography of course!), this is one more "astro"-photo related with our parent star''s destiny. There was not muct post processing at this image, Mainly the camera''s settings helped to capture this specific view. But you can''t imagine how impressive and spectacular it was in my eyes also. The clouds were moving just at the edge of the road, and Sun''s light gave them an orange color... amazing. Fortunately I was lucky enough to keep this moment!', '2006-01-19 05:12:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2058527, 276169, 50568, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for all your good comments!<br/>It has been taken in Paris, at "place de la Concorde", at sunset.  I was standing on "l''avenue des champs élysées". There were a lot of tourists and trafic in town (taken december 31).</td>', 'Thanks everyone for all your good comments!It has been taken in Paris, at "place de la Concorde", at sunset.  I was standing on "l''avenue des champs élysées". There were a lot of tourists and trafic in town (taken december 31).', '2006-01-19 08:40:28.000000', NULL, 0),
